# linux-firmware-full: install every firmware family.
#
# The linux-firmware package itself ships licence evidence only
# (WHENCE + LICENSES). The blobs live in seven family splits:
#
#   linux-firmware-intel    iwlwifi/BT (377M)
#   linux-firmware-i915     Intel integrated + xe discrete GPU (33M)
#   linux-firmware-amd      amdgpu/radeon/microcode (121M)
#   linux-firmware-nvidia   NVIDIA GPU/networking (152M)
#   linux-firmware-qcom     Qualcomm SoC/adreno/modem (524M)
#   linux-firmware-network  all NICs/WLAN (mellanox, netronome, mrvl,
#                           mediatek, ath*, brcm, realtek, ... ~600M)
#   linux-firmware-misc     audio/video/USB-serial/SoC leftovers
#
# Minimal hosts install only the families their hardware needs;
# installer images (unknown hardware) install this meta package.
# Snapshot gap (pre-existing, upstream): no intel-ucode ships in the
# 20260910 snapshot, so Intel microcode updates are absent from every
# split. amd-ucode rides in linux-firmware-amd.
